<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. weekend box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. weekend box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the studios' estimates for the top 10 movies for the Feb. 21-23 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    1 (*) The Empire Strikes Back ........  $22.4 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Star Wars ....................... $11.0 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Absolute Power ..................  $9.0 million</p>
<p>    4 (3) Dante's Peak ....................  $7.0 million</p>
<p>    5 (4) Vegas Vacation ..................  $6.6 million</p>
<p>    6 (5) Fools Rush In ...................  $5.6 million</p>
<p>    7 (6) That Darn Cat ...................  $3.6 million</p>
<p>    8 (*) Rosewood ........................  $3.2 million</p>
<p>    9 (7) Jerry Maguire ...................  $3.1 million</p>
<p>    10(8) The English Patient .............  $2.8 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's figures in parenthesis.</p>
<p>&quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; and &quot;Star Wars&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Absolute Power,&quot; &quot;Fools Rush In&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Vegas Vacation&quot; and &quot;Rosewood&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;That Darn Cat&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney.</p>
